\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Planar radial vectors from the origin $O=(0,0)$, head-to-tail polygon closure, and the Diophantine Pell minimum at order four. (a)~The $16$ radial vectors $z_{ij}\mathbf  r_{ij}$ radiating from $O$ (orange $z_{ij}>0$ outward, blue $z_{ij}<0$ inward) across the three concentric rings $R_{\mathrm  {in}},R_{\mathrm  {mid}},R_{\mathrm  {out}}$ on square \#70, together with the three ring dipole resultants $\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {in}}=(3,0)$, $\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {out}}=(15,0)$, and $\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {mid}}=(-18,0)$. (b)~Placing the $16$ vectors $z_{ij}\ell (r_{ij})\mathbf  u_{ij}$ head-to-tail in order of angle around $O$ produces a closed $16$-gon at linear lengths $\alpha =1$ ($\ell (r)=r$ on \#70, solid orange/blue) and at inverse radial lengths $\alpha ^*=-1$ ($\ell (r)=1/r$ on \#45, green dash-dot), whereas unit lengths $\alpha =0$ ($\ell (r)=1$ on \#635, dashed) fail to close by the magenta gap vector $\mathbf  B_{\mathrm  {unit}}(S)$. (c)~Scatter plot of $\|\mathbf  v(S)\|_2=\|\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {in}}+\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {out}}\|_2$ versus $\|\mathbf  u(S)\|_2=\|\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {in}}+\frac  13\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {out}}\|_2$ across all $880$ magic squares against the irrational balance line $\|\mathbf  v\|=\sqrt  {5}\,\|\mathbf  u\|$, with the eight Pell-minimum squares ($v/u=9/4$) marked by red stars. (d)~Resultant norm $\|\mathbf  B_{z,r^\alpha }(S)\|_2$ versus power-law exponent $\alpha $, highlighting the universal root at $\alpha =1$ and the exact second roots at $\alpha ^*=-1$ (\#45, $\kappa =+9$), $\alpha ^*=-0.050$ (\#70, $\kappa =+5$), and $\alpha ^*=+3$ (\#286, $\kappa =+1$).}}{6}{figure.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ring-vectors}{{2}{6}{Planar radial vectors from the origin $O=(0,0)$, head-to-tail polygon closure, and the Diophantine Pell minimum at order four. (a)~The $16$ radial vectors $z_{ij}\mathbf r_{ij}$ radiating from $O$ (orange $z_{ij}>0$ outward, blue $z_{ij}<0$ inward) across the three concentric rings $R_{\mathrm {in}},R_{\mathrm {mid}},R_{\mathrm {out}}$ on square \#70, together with the three ring dipole resultants $\mathbf d_{\mathrm {in}}=(3,0)$, $\mathbf d_{\mathrm {out}}=(15,0)$, and $\mathbf d_{\mathrm {mid}}=(-18,0)$. (b)~Placing the $16$ vectors $z_{ij}\ell (r_{ij})\mathbf u_{ij}$ head-to-tail in order of angle around $O$ produces a closed $16$-gon at linear lengths $\alpha =1$ ($\ell (r)=r$ on \#70, solid orange/blue) and at inverse radial lengths $\alpha ^*=-1$ ($\ell (r)=1/r$ on \#45, green dash-dot), whereas unit lengths $\alpha =0$ ($\ell (r)=1$ on \#635, dashed) fail to close by the magenta gap vector $\mathbf B_{\mathrm {unit}}(S)$. (c)~Scatter plot of $\|\mathbf v(S)\|_2=\|\mathbf d_{\mathrm {in}}+\mathbf d_{\mathrm {out}}\|_2$ versus $\|\mathbf u(S)\|_2=\|\mathbf d_{\mathrm {in}}+\frac 13\mathbf d_{\mathrm {out}}\|_2$ across all $880$ magic squares against the irrational balance line $\|\mathbf v\|=\sqrt {5}\,\|\mathbf u\|$, with the eight Pell-minimum squares ($v/u=9/4$) marked by red stars. (d)~Resultant norm $\|\mathbf B_{z,r^\alpha }(S)\|_2$ versus power-law exponent $\alpha $, highlighting the universal root at $\alpha =1$ and the exact second roots at $\alpha ^*=-1$ (\#45, $\kappa =+9$), $\alpha ^*=-0.050$ (\#70, $\kappa =+5$), and $\alpha ^*=+3$ (\#286, $\kappa =+1$)}{figure.16}{}}
